# Code of Conduct

## Commitment

We are committed to a welcoming, safe, and equitable community for everyone
who participates in good faith.

## Expected behavior

- Engage honestly, respectfully, and constructively.
- Respect different experiences, viewpoints, and communication styles.
- Give and receive technical feedback without personal attacks.
- Take responsibility for mistakes and work to repair harm.
- Respect privacy, boundaries, and confidential information.

## Unacceptable behavior

- Harassment, intimidation, threats, or unwanted personal attention.
- Discrimination, stereotyping, sexualization, or demeaning language.
- Publishing another person's private information without permission.
- Impersonation or evasion of moderation actions.
- Deliberate disruption, trolling, or retaliation.

## Scope

This policy applies in repository issues, pull requests, reviews, discussions,
commits, and other project spaces. It also applies when someone officially
represents the project elsewhere.

## Reporting

[% if github_owner %]
Report possible violations privately to
[@[[ github_owner | trim | regex_replace('^@', '') ]]](https://github.com/[[ github_owner | trim | regex_replace('^@', '') ]]).
[% else %]
Report possible violations through a private maintainer channel. Do not publish
sensitive incident details in an issue.
[% endif %]

Maintainers may remove content, restrict participation, issue warnings,
suspend access, or permanently ban a participant. Responses will be
proportionate to the impact, pattern, and severity of the behavior.

